# Set the position gains of the 6 arm joints (<arm>/set_arm_gains).
# gains.kp / gains.kd: each either 6 values or EMPTY (= the arm's configured
# value for that list). Both empty = back to the configured gains.
#   kp: N*m/rad, finite, > 0.   kd: N*m*s/rad, finite, > 0.
# Each value is CLAMPED per joint: kp into [stock / 8, stock], kd into
# [stock / sqrt(8), stock]. The response carries what was applied.
ccros_msgs/ArmGains gains
# The caller's fully-qualified node name. While the gains are in force the
# driver checks about once a second that this node is still in the ROS graph
# and restores the configured gains once it is gone. Empty = no watch.
string owner
---
bool ok
string error
float64[] applied_kp   # N*m/rad
float64[] applied_kd   # N*m*s/rad
